+From fe25b9de1cf2de4ed9220f94af03dd0b4c1c5c1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:45:59 +0800
+Subject: [PATCH 01/40] arm64: kernel: Keep .bss.rtic inside the image
+
+The vendor linker script puts the RTIC bss block (which holds selinux_state)
+after the zero-address debug sections.  binutils 2.27 merges it into .bss so
+the factory image is fine, but GNU ld 2.38 and lld either fail to link
+("relocation truncated to fit: R_AARCH64_ADR_PREL_PG_HI21") or place it after
+_end, where the page allocator overwrites selinux_state and the device hangs on
+the very first screen (verified with nm: selinux_state == _end).
+
+Move the block to after BSS_SECTION() and before _end, and keep the kernel
+release at exactly 4.14.190-perf so the vendor DLKM vermagic keeps matching.
+
+Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
+---
+ EEBBK_S6_changes.md             | 89 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
+ arch/arm64/kernel/vmlinux.lds.S | 28 ++++++-----
+ 2 files changed, 98 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)
