+From fb705bbaa5b221d4f2c2f2b322bbd60df2c5afc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:24:54 +0800
+Subject: [PATCH 02/40] module: Accept vendor DLKM signature and symbol CRC
+ mismatches
+
+The vendor modules in /vendor/lib/modules are built from the complete vendor
+tree together with the shipping kernel, so a kernel built from this tree cannot
+match their signature or their symbol CRCs (module_layout: vendor 0xcc8cac52,
+this tree 0x021f9ae4).
+
+CONFIG_MODVERSIONS cannot be disabled because "modversions" is part of the
+vermagic string ("4.14.190-perf SMP preempt mod_unload modversions aarch64"), so
+relax the two checks instead:
+
+  - CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE=n in the generated .config, and
+  - check_version() only warns and accepts on a CRC mismatch, which is what
+    modprobe --force would do.
+
+On hardware this took lsmod from 1 to 35 modules and stopped the vendor audio
+HAL from crashing in get_sndcard_id().
+
+Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
